  "id": "COMPOUND:27962 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanistic link between n-Octyl sulfate and RWLeu4, through a series of target interactions. n-Octyl sulfate is implicated in targeting multiple enzymes, including CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in sialylation pathways. This enzyme is subsequently targeted by a compound with the structure (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, which in turn has a target of RWLeu4. The presence of multiple intermediate targets indicates a possible pathway where n-Octyl sulfate may influence the activity of these enzymes, potentially affecting the production or function of RWLeu4. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of n-Octyl sulfate in the regulation of RWLeu4.",
